NOTE: session closed (PR merged/closed) — this commit is LOCAL; push from a new session.

- CRITICAL: disbursement JE direction was inverted (bank debited on payment → ledger showed money IN) — now debit counterpart / credit bank
- CRITICAL regression catcher: voucher routes passed account CODES ('2110') as account_id — every voucher POST would crash after Section 3's insertJournalLines enforcement; codes now resolve to real company-scoped account ids
- Receipt POST had a copy-pasted insufficient-balance check (receipts ADD money) — removed
- Voucher PUT (edit) hard-deleted the original JE and could post UNBALANCED entries; now: reversal (original kept) + new balanced JE; disbursement [id] PUT didn't exist at all (frontend edit → 405) — implemented
- Voucher DELETE destroyed JE + allocation links materalized; now soft-cancel (status='cancelled') + reversal + allocation revert (invoice paid trio restored)
- Invoice allocation implemented per dormant schema design: receipt→invoices, disbursement→purchase_invoices via link tables, capped at remaining, allocations > voucher amount rejected, contact match enforced, full rollback on failure
- Receipt collection route: broken DELETE handler removed (params-less); GET lists exclude cancelled; disbursement GET returns 'disbursements' key (frontend read it — list always empty)
- Banks: auto sub-account code was timestamp-4 (two banks within ~10s shared ONE ledger account) — sequential unique; type/name validated; balance reads company-scoped
- banks/[id] opening-balance edit targeted the company's LATEST opening entry (possibly ANOTHER bank's) and deleted only the bank line (unbalanced JE!) — now targets the bank's own entry, rewrites BOTH sides, requires capital account
- Bank reconciliation: bank tenant check, numeric closing balance, status enum
- src/lib/voucher-utils.ts: postReversalEntry / resolveAccountId / applyInvoiceAllocations / revertInvoiceAllocations
- 18 new tests (vouchers-integrity.test.ts); suite 213/213, tsc clean, eslint 0 errors

